{:mulog/duration 229750, :mulog/namespace "ai.obney.grain.event-store-v3.core.in-memory", :grain/event-ids (#uuid "019e4320-665f-707c-84de-e4b670e07acc" #uuid "019e4320-665f-707d-8fda-00472b683540" #uuid "019e4320-665d-7015-a6cd-1fa6070a0cd1"), :mulog/outcome :ok, :mulog/parent-trace #mulog/flake "5A3YlH5doGhfr2iytBIz708a-G3bSCfC", :mulog/root-trace #mulog/flake "5A3YlH5doGhfr2iytBIz708a-G3bSCfC", :mulog/timestamp 1779242657376, :metric/name "GrainAppendEvents", :mulog/trace-id #mulog/flake "5A3YlH7P2uM6CYUFd45iWjfX_xzTaRnM", :mulog/event-name :ai.obney.grain.event-store-v3.core.in-memory/append}
{:mulog/duration 7865750, :mulog/namespace "ai.obney.grain.command-processor-v2.core", :mulog/outcome :ok, :mulog/parent-trace nil, :ai.obney.grain.command-processor-v2.core/command {:tick-id #uuid "96664ad4-ce7f-4e10-babc-496d1436e315", :writes {:major-changes "1. **MAJOR: Removal of Domestic Content Requirements.** (Sections B(5)(iv), 4.4.4, 6.5, and Appendix C). The obligation to source 60% of solar PV components domestically, and the associated grids for calculation, have been entirely eliminated.\n2. **MAJOR: Data Disclosure Expansion.** (Section 6.5). New authorization for OPA to share Facility data with third-party government ministries and emergency services for public health/safety planning.\n3. **MINOR: Standardization of Administrative Actions.** (Sections 5.1.2, 7.2, 8.1, 9, and Appendix A). All notices, changes, and amendments must now strictly use a \"Prescribed Form\" as defined by the OPA website.\n4. **MINOR: OPA Discretionary Waivers.** (Appendix A \"Project Eligibility\" and Appendix C \"Existing Building\"). OPA granted \"sole and absolute discretion\" to waive certain eligibility requirements or deem buildings as \"Existing\" in writing.\n5. **COSMETIC: Version Revision and Renumbering.** (Part 1 and Section 4.4). Branding change to v3.1.1 and sequential update of 4.4.x clauses following removals.", :impact-analysis "1. **Domestic Content Removal:**\n   * **Affected Party:** Supplier.\n   * **Risk Shift:** Significant reduction in financial and compliance risk for the Supplier. Suppliers are no longer restricted to local supply chains, allowing for lower-cost global procurement and eliminating the risk of default due to failure to meet the 60% threshold.\n2. **Expansion of Data Disclosure:**\n   * **Affected Party:** Supplier.\n   * **Risk Shift:** Shift toward OPA. Suppliers lose a degree of privacy regarding facility details, as the OPA gains broad rights to share information with secondary government agencies without further Supplier consent.\n3. **Prescribed Form Requirements:**\n   * **Affected Party:** Supplier.\n   * **Risk Shift:** Shift toward OPA. While clarifying the process, this limits Supplier flexibility. Failure to use the exact version of a form found on the website could result in administrative rejection of notices or amendments, placing the burden of \"form monitoring\" on the Supplier.\n4. **Discretionary Eligibility Power:**\n   * **Affected Party:** OPA (Beneficiary) / Supplier (Applicant).\n   * **Risk Shift:** Increased power for OPA. By adding \"sole and absolute discretion\" for eligibility and building definitions, the OPA gains the legal shield to approve or deny projects that fall into grey areas without being subject to \"reasonableness\" challenges, though it creates a potential pathway for Suppliers who otherwise would be ineligible."}, :command/name :sheet/complete-node-execution, :command/timestamp #time/offset-date-time "2026-05-19T21:04:17.368599-05:00", :command/id #uuid "a7a13ad5-8f11-42e8-ae50-cfc1f2bd7d80", :duration-ms 8416, :usage {:prompt-tokens 1032, :completion-tokens 1394, :total-tokens 2426}, :status :success, :node-id #uuid "b23d21f5-2db0-43cc-bc20-a13dd8117f51", :sheet-id #uuid "0883af44-f395-4c1b-a9e3-f3bd031daece"}, :mulog/root-trace #mulog/flake "5A3YlH5doGhfr2iytBIz708a-G3bSCfC", :mulog/timestamp 1779242657368, :metric/name "CommandProcessed", :mulog/trace-id #mulog/flake "5A3YlH5doGhfr2iytBIz708a-G3bSCfC", :mulog/event-name :ai.obney.grain.command-processor-v2.core/process-command, :metric/resolution :high}
