{:mulog/duration 848417, :mulog/namespace "ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core", :mulog/outcome :ok, :mulog/parent-trace nil, :event {:tick-id #uuid "96664ad4-ce7f-4e10-babc-496d1436e315", :event/tags #{[:sheet #uuid "0883af44-f395-4c1b-a9e3-f3bd031daece"] [:node #uuid "b5142f81-0d9a-4e1f-a280-305d86efa30a"] [:tick #uuid "96664ad4-ce7f-4e10-babc-496d1436e315"]}, :event/timestamp #time/offset-date-time "2026-05-19T21:04:17.383392-05:00", :inputs {:major-changes "1. **MAJOR: Removal of Domestic Content Requirements.** (Sections B(5)(iv), 4.4.4, 6.5, and Appendix C). The obligation to source 60% of solar PV components domestically, and the associated grids for calculation, have been entirely eliminated.\n2. **MAJOR: Data Disclosure Expansion.** (Section 6.5). New authorization for OPA to share Facility data with third-party government ministries and emergency services for public health/safety planning.\n3. **MINOR: Standardization of Administrative Actions.** (Sections 5.1.2, 7.2, 8.1, 9, and Appendix A). All notices, changes, and amendments must now strictly use a \"Prescribed Form\" as defined by the OPA website.\n4. **MINOR: OPA Discretionary Waivers.** (Appendix A \"Project Eligibility\" and Appendix C \"Existing Building\"). OPA granted \"sole and absolute discretion\" to waive certain eligibility requirements or deem buildings as \"Existing\" in writing.\n5. **COSMETIC: Version Revision and Renumbering.** (Part 1 and Section 4.4). Branding change to v3.1.1 and sequential update of 4.4.x clauses following removals.", :impact-analysis "1. **Domestic Content Removal:**\n   * **Affected Party:** Supplier.\n   * **Risk Shift:** Significant reduction in financial and compliance risk for the Supplier. Suppliers are no longer restricted to local supply chains, allowing for lower-cost global procurement and eliminating the risk of default due to failure to meet the 60% threshold.\n2. **Expansion of Data Disclosure:**\n   * **Affected Party:** Supplier.\n   * **Risk Shift:** Shift toward OPA. Suppliers lose a degree of privacy regarding facility details, as the OPA gains broad rights to share information with secondary government agencies without further Supplier consent.\n3. **Prescribed Form Requirements:**\n   * **Affected Party:** Supplier.\n   * **Risk Shift:** Shift toward OPA. While clarifying the process, this limits Supplier flexibility. Failure to use the exact version of a form found on the website could result in administrative rejection of notices or amendments, placing the burden of \"form monitoring\" on the Supplier.\n4. **Discretionary Eligibility Power:**\n   * **Affected Party:** OPA (Beneficiary) / Supplier (Applicant).\n   * **Risk Shift:** Increased power for OPA. By adding \"sole and absolute discretion\" for eligibility and building definitions, the OPA gains the legal shield to approve or deny projects that fall into grey areas without being subject to \"reasonableness\" challenges, though it creates a potential pathway for Suppliers who otherwise would be ineligible.", :section-diffs "The following represents a comprehensive list of additions, removals, and wording changes between `contract_v2` (Version 2.0) and `contract_v3` (Version 3.1.1).\n\n### **Part 1 – Contract Details**\n*   **Version Number:** Changed from \"Version 2.0\" to \"Version 3.1.1\".\n*   **Section B(5)(iv):** **Removed.** The requirement for a \"Minimum Required Domestic Content Level\" of 60% for solar PV has been deleted.\n*   **Section C:** **No changes.** (The optionality for Appendix B remains).\n\n### **Part 2 – General Terms and Conditions**\n*   **Section 2 through 4.3:** **No changes.**\n*   **Section 4.4.4:** **Removed.** The representation regarding \"Domestic Content Level\" has been deleted. (Subsequent subsections 4.4.5 and 4.4.6 in v2.0 are renumbered to 4.4.4 and 4.4.5 in v3.1.1).\n*   **Section 5.1.2:** **Wording Change.** Added the requirement that notification of changes must be \"in the Prescribed Form\".\n*   **Section 6.5 (Collection of Information):** **Wording Change.** Removed the requirement to collect information to \"establish compliance with Minimum Required Domestic Content Level\".\n*   **Section 6.5 (Disclosure of Information):** \n    *   **Removal:** Removed disclosure of \"compliance with Minimum Required Domestic Content Level\".\n    *   **Addition:** Added a new provision allowing OPA to disclose Facility details to government ministries/agencies for purposes of \"promoting public health and safety\" and \"emergency services personnel\" planning.\n*   **Section 7.2:** **Wording Change.** Added that change of contact information notice must be \"in the Prescribed Form\".\n*   **Section 8.1:** **Wording Change.** Added that termination notice must be \"in the Prescribed Form\".\n*   **Section 9:** **Wording Change.** Added that amendments must be reduced to writing \"in the Prescribed Form\".\n\n### **Appendix A – Definitions**\n*   **Added Definition:** `“Prescribed Form”` (Latest version of a form appearing on the Website).\n*   **Added Definition:** `“Website”` (The OPA's microFIT Program URL).\n*   **Removed Definition:** `“Domestic Content Level”`.\n*   **Removed Definition:** `“Minimum Required Domestic Content Level”`.\n*   **Project Eligibility Requirements (Definition):**\n    *   **Section (c):** **Wording Change.** Added qualifying text: \"unless otherwise consented to by the OPA in writing in its sole and absolute discretion\".\n\n### **Appendix B – Calculation of Indexed Contract Price**\n*   **No changes.**\n\n### **Appendix C – Solar PV Schedule**\n*   **Additional Defined Terms:** \n    *   `“Existing Building”`: **Wording Change.** Added part (b) allowing OPA \"sole and absolute discretion\" to issue written confirmation deeming a building as an \"Existing Building\".\n*   **Domestic Content Requirements:** **Entirely Removed.** Sections 1.1 through 1.7 and Tables 1, 2, and 3 (Domestic Content Grids for Crystalline Silicon, Thin-Film, and Concentrated PV) which appeared in v2.0 are completely deleted in v3.1.1.\n\n### **Appendix D-1, D-2, and E**\n*   **No changes** (outside of minor formatting or carry-over defined term impacts)."}, :node-id #uuid "b5142f81-0d9a-4e1f-a280-305d86efa30a", :event/type :sheet/node-execution-started, :sheet-id #uuid "0883af44-f395-4c1b-a9e3-f3bd031daece", :event/id #uuid "019e4320-6667-706f-a4ec-60358261a6f4"}, :mulog/root-trace #mulog/flake "5A3YlH9HcSgR00-tYQF5dm1mAdt2cWEx", :mulog/timestamp 1779242657384, :metric/name "TodoProcessed", :mulog/trace-id #mulog/flake "5A3YlH9HcSgR00-tYQF5dm1mAdt2cWEx", :mulog/event-name :ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core/processing-event, :metric/resolution :high}
